# Build context for deploy/Dockerfile (`docker build .` from backend/).
#
# The backend Dockerfile uses explicit `COPY --link <dir>/ <dir>/` for
# each tree it actually needs (cmd/, internal/, migrations/, proto/,
# go.mod, go.sum, buf*.yaml, sqlc.yaml). So .dockerignore here doesn't
# decide what lands in the *image* — that's already pinned by the
# Dockerfile. What it does decide is the size of the build context the
# Docker daemon receives. Excluding the obvious junk (.git, tests/,
# bin/, agent caches) takes the context from ~hundreds of MB down to
# the source files that matter, which speeds every uncached build.

# ── Self-reference ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
.dockerignore
deploy/Dockerfile
deploy/docker-compose.yaml
deploy/chart/

# ── VCS / CI metadata ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/

# ── Build artifacts (Go output anywhere in the tree) ────────────────
bin/
out/
dist/
*.test
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# ── Coverage / profile output ───────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
*.out
profile.cov

# ── Tests trees we never need at build time ─────────────────────────
# These live in backend/tests/ but are exercised by `go test ./...`
# and out-of-band Hurl / grpcurl harnesses — never by `go build`. The
# `internal/` tree IS copied (the Go compiler needs it for the
# package graph); these external tests are not.
tests/grpcurl/reports/
tests/api/mutations/reports/
tests/api/security/reports/
tests/integration/testdata/

# ── Secrets / local-only ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Runtime configs are mounted via Helm ConfigMap or compose bind
# mount, never baked in — exclude every dev-only artifact under
# configs/local/ plus any stray dotenv. Keep configs/config.yaml
# (the schema reference) so docs builds can render it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
configs/local/

# ── Editor / OS / agent detritus ────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.claude/
.agents/

# ── Logs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log

# ── Repo-tooling configs not needed at build time ───────────────────
.golangci.yaml
.mockery.yaml
lefthook.yml
README.md
CHANGELOG.md
CLAUDE.md
skills-lock.json
docs/
scripts/

# ── Trees the Dockerfile doesn't COPY ───────────────────────────────
# These are real source dirs, but the binary build doesn't reach
# them: `pkg/` exposes the public Connect SDK to external consumers
# (image carries internal/api/pb/... already), `policies/` ships
# Cedar policy fixtures used by tests + docs, `tasks/` and
# Taskfile.yaml are the developer-side build orchestrator. Excluding
# them keeps the context tight; if a future Dockerfile starts to
# COPY one of these, drop the matching entry here.
pkg/
policies/
tasks/
Taskfile.yaml
tools.go
